  "0{Troll Rogue:} Berserking (+10% haste), Rapid Regeneration (50% HP in 6 s, no corpse needed), Regeneration (20% regen in combat), Beast Slaying (+5% vs Beast). Warcraft Tavern: second in Horde PvE; Rogue's Diary: 'less downtime than almost everyone'.",
  "0{Troll Shaman:} Berserking +10% cast and attack speed for 15 s (increased Oct 27), Rapid Regeneration (50% Health over time), Beast Slaying +5% to Beasts, Regeneration 10% in combat. Rankedboost (snippet): A.",
  "Gan'rul's Summons (Orc/Troll, level 10): talk to Ophek in Razor Hill, then to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar. Then Creature of the Void: recover the Tablet of Verga for Gan'rul (Skull Rock ). Then The Binding: use the Glyphs of Summoning to summon and subjugate a Voidwalker, bring the glyphs back to Gan'rul. Reward: Summon Voidwalker .",
  "0{Troll Warlock:} Troll (Horde, new Warlock ): Berserking (+10% haste, doesn't apply to DoTs), Rapid Regeneration (channel that heals, great with Life Tap), Regeneration (HP regen in combat), Beast Slaying (+5% damage to Beasts, useful in the Barrens). Method: tier C. Starts in the Valley of Trials like the Orc.",
  "0{Troll Warrior:} Berserking +10% attack/cast speed for 15 s (3 min CD; nerf from Classic's 30%), Beast Slaying +5% damage to Beasts, Regeneration (20% from Oct 16 ), Rapid Regeneration (channeled).",
  "1. Camp Narache",
  "2. Bloodhoof Village",
  "3. Thunder Bluff",
  "^spell_nature_regeneration^Trainer: Mark of the Wild, Wrath, Healing Touch",
  "Class trainer Tauren: Gart Mistrunner (Red Cloud Mesa, Mulgore) or Gennia Runetotem (Bloodhoof Village).",
  "^spell_nature_starfall^Trainer: Moonfire, Rejuvenation",
  "6-slot bag (Grace of An'she and Mu'sha): Seer Graytongue, Red Cloud Mesa. Bring the incense to the shrine before the timer runs out.",
  "The Adventurer (Chief Hawkwind, Camp Narache, lvl 6), then The Great Outdoors (Kaga Wildhoof, Bloodhoof Village): unlocks Camping.",
  "^spell_nature_thorns^Trainer: Thorns",
  "Camping 101: Cooking from Kaga Wildhoof: unlocks Basic Campfire.",
  "^spell_nature_stranglevines^Trainer: Entangling Roots",
  "^ability_racial_bearform^Trainer: Bear Form, Growl, Maul, Demoralizing Roar, Nature's Grasp, Teleport: Moonglade",
  "Heeding the Call (Tauren, level 10): talk to Gennia Runetotem in Bloodhoof Village. Then talk to Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Reward: Bear Form.",
  "^spell_nature_resistnature^Trainer: Regrowth, Revive, Enrage",
  "^spell_nature_nullifypoison^Trainer: Cure Poison, Bash",
  "Cozy Sleeping Bag: long, optional chain.",
  "Lessons Anew (Tauren, level 14, Cure Poison): talk to Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise. Use Teleport: Moonglade and talk to Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven. Reward: Cure Poison .",
  "^ability_druid_aquaticform^Trainer: Aquatic Form, Swipe",
  "A Lesson to Learn (Tauren, level 16, Aquatic Form): talk to Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise. Use Teleport: Moonglade and talk to Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven. Reward: Aquatic Form (Idol of Shifting Tides ).",
  "^spell_nature_faeriefire^Trainer: Faerie Fire, Hibernate",
  "^ability_druid_catform^Trainer: Cat Form, Claw, Prowl, Rip, Shred, Starfire, Rebirth, Omen of Clarity, Polearms",
  "The Great Cat Spirit (Tauren, level 20, Cat Form): talk to Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise. Use Teleport: Moonglade and talk to Dendrite Starblaze. Go to the south of Moonglade to the Great Cat Spirit. Retrieve the three relics at Stormrage Barrow Den and bring them back to the spirit. Reward: Cat Form .",
  "^ability_hunter_beastsoothe^Trainer: Soothe Animal",
  "^spell_nature_removecurse^Trainer: Remove Curse, Rake, Tiger's Fury, Ferocious Bite",
  "^ability_druid_dash^Trainer: Dash, Abolish Poison",
  "^ability_druid_cower^Trainer: Cower, Challenging Roar",
  "^ability_druid_supriseattack^Trainer: Pounce, Frenzied Regeneration",
